1103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 256 0 R
/E (IP spoofing is a technique where an attacker forges the source IP address in network packets to impersonate another system. It is commonly used in attacks such as DDoS, session hijacking, and bypassing IP-based authentication. This experiment demonstrates IP spoofing using a publicly available GitHub tool to understand how attackers manipulate packet headers. Kali Linux provides a safe and controlled environment for ethical network security experimentation. )
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
